---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Between Two Gates — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 121"
  description="Chullin 121: a validly slaughtered animal is still twitching — out of the category of the living, not yet entered the category of the dead. Rule ten real laws at the threshold: food impurity but not carcass impurity, the limb that parts versus the flesh that parts, Abaye's double stringency, and the trap of the invalid slaughter. Probe the bird and the beast for the parts that are 'merely wood,' and judge which gathering of alal carries carcass impurity."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@600;700&family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0a0b14] !text-[#e2e5f0]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#252a42] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#141830] to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#a78bfa]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#c4b5fd]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 121 · 2026-09-02
      </p>
      <h1 class="cormorant text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">🚪 Between Two Gates</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-3 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f0954f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">יָצְתָה מִכְּלַל חַיָּה, וְלִכְלַל מֵתָה לֹא בָּאת</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-1 text-xs italic !text-[#7c86a6]">
        "It has left the category of the living, but has not entered the category of the dead." — Rabbi Zeira, Chullin 121b
      </p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#aab1c9]">
        The knife has done its work — both simanim cut, a valid slaughter — but the animal is still
        twitching. Is it alive? Is it dead? Chullin 121 answers: <i>neither</i>. For each law you must
        decide which world claims it: it takes the impurity of food but not of a carcass; a limb that
        parts from it parts from the living; a gentile may not eat it. Stand at the threshold and rule.
        But first — probe the bird and the beast for the parts that are merely wood.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Score strip ============ -->
      <div class="sticky top-2 z-20 mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f]/95 px-4 py-2.5 text-center shadow-lg shadow-black/40 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#7c86a6]">first-try verdicts</span>
        <span id="score" class="cormorant ml-2 text-base font-bold !text-[#f0954f]">0 / 19</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Act I: Merely Wood ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act1-h">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#a78bfa]">act i · the probe</p>
        <h2 id="act1-h" class="cormorant mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e2e5f0]">עֵץ בְּעָלְמָא — it is merely wood</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#aab1c9]">
          The mishnayot say the beak, the talons, and the horns <i>join</i> with the flesh toward the
          egg-bulk of food impurity. The Gemara objects: they're wood! Rabbi Elazar and Rav Pappa
          locate the living seam in each. Press a pin, then rule: does that part join — or is it
          merely wood?
        </p>
        <div id="probe-panels" class="mt-5 space-y-4"></div>
        <div id="probe-card" class="mt-4"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act II: The Threshold ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act2-h" class="mt-14">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#a78bfa]">act ii · the threshold</p>
        <h2 id="act2-h" class="cormorant mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e2e5f0]">The animal that stands in the doorway</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#aab1c9]">
          A Jew slaughters a non-kosher animal for a gentile — or a gentile slaughters a kosher animal
          for a Jew. Two simanim cut, a valid slaughter, and it is still twitching
          (<i>mefarkeset</i>). Rav Oshaya's baraita walks through its laws one by one. For each,
          choose the gate: does the law treat it as <b class="!text-[#f0954f]">living</b> or as
          <b class="!text-[#9db1c7]">dead</b>? And beware — for some cases the doorway itself collapses.
        </p>

        <!-- the doorway -->
        <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] px-3 py-5">
          <div class="relative mx-auto flex h-28 max-w-lg items-stretch justify-between">
            <!-- living gate -->
            <div class="flex w-16 flex-col items-center justify-between rounded-xl border border-[#f0954f]/50 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#2a1a10] to-[#171a2b] py-2 sm:w-20">
              <span class="text-lg" aria-hidden="true">🔥</span>
              <span class="frank text-sm font-bold !text-[#f0954f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">חַיָּה</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide !text-[#f0954f]">living <span id="tally-living">0</span></span>
            </div>
            <!-- track -->
            <div class="relative mx-2 flex-1 self-center">
              <div class="h-px w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-[#f0954f]/60 via-[#252a42] to-[#9db1c7]/60"></div>
              <div id="orb" class="orb absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2">
                <div class="orb-core frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">נֶפֶשׁ</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <!-- dead gate -->
            <div class="flex w-16 flex-col items-center justify-between rounded-xl border border-[#9db1c7]/40 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#171d26] to-[#171a2b] py-2 sm:w-20">
              <span class="text-lg" aria-hidden="true">🌫️</span>
              <span class="frank text-sm font-bold !text-[#9db1c7]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מֵתָה</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide !text-[#9db1c7]">dead <span id="tally-dead">0</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="orb-caption" class="mt-3 text-center text-[11px] italic !text-[#7c86a6]" aria-live="polite">
            The soul has not yet departed. Every ruling tugs it toward a gate — watch where it settles.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="threshold-cards" class="mt-5 space-y-4"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act III: The Collectors ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act3-h" class="mt-14">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#a78bfa]">act iii · the collectors</p>
        <h2 id="act3-h" class="cormorant mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e2e5f0]">The alal on the hide</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#aab1c9]">
          What is the <i>alal</i> of the mishna? Rabbi Yoḥanan says the nuchal ligament
          (<i>marteka</i>) — the cord Job's "physicians of no value" (<i>elil</i>) pretend to heal.
          Reish Lakish says: בָּשָׂר שֶׁפְּלָטַתּוּ סַכִּין — flesh the flaying knife spat onto the hide. For
          Rabbi Yehuda's ruling below, all agree it is the knife-flayed residue; scraps of meat left
          clinging to the skin, food-status nullified — unless someone treats them as food again.
        </p>
        <div id="collectors" class="mt-5 space-y-4"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Finale ============ -->
      <div id="finale" class="mt-12 hidden rounded-2xl border border-[#a78bfa]/40 bg-[#141830] p-6 text-center"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#a78bfa]">learn the real daf</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#aab1c9]">
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#e2e5f0]">The opener you didn't play:</b> liquid that oozes from <i>orla</i> fruit is
            forbidden only for grapes and olives — derived by the verbal analogy "fruit"/"fruit" from first fruits
            (<a class="!text-[#f0954f] underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.121a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">121a:1</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#e2e5f0]">Why does the twitching animal need contact with liquid?</b> Any food headed for a
            more severe impurity needs no <i>hechsher</i> — like the kosher-bird carcass that will defile in the very
            throat of its eater (Rabbi Yosei). But Ḥizkiyya answers: the slaughterer could chop this animal down to
            pieces smaller than an olive-bulk, so its severe impurity is never certain
            (<a class="!text-[#f0954f] underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.121a.17" target="_blank" rel="noopener">121a:17–121b:2</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#e2e5f0]">Relay slaughter:</b> a gentile cuts half the windpipe — not enough to make the
            animal a <i>tereifa</i> — and a Jew finishes: kosher. A Jew begins and a gentile finishes: invalid
            (<a class="!text-[#f0954f] underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.121b.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">121b:13–14</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#e2e5f0]">The remedy at the neck:</b> "One who wishes to be healthy" cuts an olive-bulk from
            the place of slaughter before the soul departs, salts it very well, rinses it very well, waits for death —
            and then Jew and gentile alike may eat it (Rav Idi bar Avin in the name of Rav Yitzḥak bar Ashyan)
            (<a class="!text-[#f0954f] underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.121b.15" target="_blank" rel="noopener">121b:15–16</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#e2e5f0]">Go deeper:</b>
            <a class="!text-[#f0954f] underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.121a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read Chullin 121 on Sefaria</a>
            with its most-linked commentaries: Rashi (58 links), Steinsaltz (42), Jastrow (17), Tosafot (12), and
            Rambam's Hilchot Tum'at Ochlin (10).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-center text-[11px] !text-[#565d78]">
        <a href="/daf" class="underline hover:!text-[#7c86a6]">← back to the daf yomi arcade</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .cormorant { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; }
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #a78bfa; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .orb { transition: transform 1s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.3, 0.5, 1), opacity 0.5s ease; }
    .orb-core {
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: 9999px;
      font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #ffd9b8 !important;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #f0954f 0%, #7a3d1e 65%, #2a1a10 100%);
      box-shadow: 0 0 18px 4px rgba(240, 149, 79, 0.35);
      animation: heartbeat 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    .orb.dimmed .orb-core { opacity: 0.25; box-shadow: none; animation: none; }
    @keyframes heartbeat {
      0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: 0 0 14px 3px rgba(240, 149, 79, 0.3); }
      12% { transform: scale(1.12); box-shadow: 0 0 22px 6px rgba(240, 149, 79, 0.5); }
      24% { transform: scale(1); }
      36% { transform: scale(1.08); }
      48% { transform: scale(1); }
    }
    .pin {
      position: absolute; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; border-radius: 9999px;
      border: 1px solid #a78bfa; background: #141830; color: #c4b5fd !important;
      font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.5); animation: pinpulse 2.2s ease-out infinite;
    }
    .pin[data-state='open'] { border-color: #e2e5f0; background: #252a42; }
    .pin[data-state='joins'] { border-color: #f0954f; background: #2a1a10; color: #f0954f !important; animation: none; }
    .pin[data-state='wood'] { border-color: #9db1c7; background: #171d26; color: #9db1c7 !important; animation: none; }
    @keyframes pinpulse {
      0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.45); }
      70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0); }
      100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(167, 139, 250, 0); }
    }
    .gate-btn { transition: background 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease; }
    .shake { animation: shake 0.35s ease; }
    @keyframes shake {
      0%, 100% { transform: translateX(0); }
      25% { transform: translateX(-5px); }
      50% { transform: translateX(5px); }
      75% { transform: translateX(-3px); }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *, .orb, .orb-core, .pin { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    // global.css forces dark text colors on h/p/li/span/div — every color utility needs !important
    const C = {
      text: '!text-[#e2e5f0]', dim: '!text-[#aab1c9]', mute: '!text-[#7c86a6]',
      ember: '!text-[#f0954f]', bone: '!text-[#9db1c7]', violet: '!text-[#a78bfa]', red: '!text-[#e05e63]',
    };
    const sef = (ref, label) =>
      `<a class="${C.ember} underline hover:!text-[#ffb36e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/${ref}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${label}</a>`;

    const TOTAL = 19;
    let score = 0, answered = 0;
    const scoreEl = document.getElementById('score');
    function bump(firstTryRight) {
      answered++;
      if (firstTryRight) score++;
      scoreEl.textContent = `${score} / ${TOTAL}`;
      maybeFinale();
    }

    // =====================================================================
    // Act I — the probe
    // =====================================================================
    const PINS = [
      { id: 'beak-tip', panel: 'bird', x: 8, y: 26, n: 1, label: 'Tip of the upper beak', joins: false,
        he: 'חַרְטוֹם — עֵץ בְּעָלְמָא הוּא',
        why: `The Gemara's own objection: the beak is merely wood — nobody eats it. The mishna in Teharot that says "the beak joins" cannot mean the hard beak.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.11', refLabel: '121a:11' },
      { id: 'mandible', panel: 'bird', x: 13, y: 42, n: 2, label: 'Lower mandible', joins: false,
        he: 'תַּחְתּוֹן נָמֵי עֵץ בְּעָלְמָא הוּא',
        why: `Rabbi Elazar first answered "the lower beak" — and the Gemara throws it straight back: the lower one is also merely wood.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.12', refLabel: '121a:12' },
      { id: 'membrane', panel: 'bird', x: 24, y: 33, n: 3, label: 'Inner membrane — the "lower of the upper"', joins: true,
        he: 'תַּחְתּוֹן שֶׁל עֶלְיוֹן',
        why: `Rav Pappa finds the seam: the lower section of the <i>upper</i> mandible — the soft membrane inside the mouth attached to the beak. That is flesh enough to join toward the egg-bulk.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.12', refLabel: '121a:12' },
      { id: 'talon-tip', panel: 'bird', x: 72, y: 82, n: 4, label: 'Horny tip of the talon', joins: false,
        he: 'עֵץ בְּעָלְמָא',
        why: `The exposed claw is inedible horn — the same "merely wood" objection. The mishna's talons cannot mean the part you can see.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.13', refLabel: '121a:13' },
      { id: 'talon-base', panel: 'bird', x: 84, y: 58, n: 5, label: 'Base of the talon, sunk in the flesh', joins: true,
        he: 'מָקוֹם הַמּוּבְלָע בַּבָּשָׂר',
        why: `Rabbi Elazar: the place subsumed within the flesh. Where the talon is swallowed by living tissue, it counts with the flesh and joins.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.13', refLabel: '121a:13' },
      { id: 'horn-shaft', panel: 'beast', x: 18, y: 22, n: 6, label: 'Shaft of the horn', joins: false,
        he: 'עֵץ בְּעָלְמָא',
        why: `Hard horn is not food. Our mishna says "the horns join" — but not this part.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.14', refLabel: '121a:14' },
      { id: 'horn-base', panel: 'beast', x: 76, y: 38, n: 7, label: 'Base of the horn, where cutting draws blood', joins: true,
        he: 'בִּמְקוֹם שֶׁחוֹתְכִין וְיוֹצֵא מֵהֶן דָּם',
        why: `Rav Pappa: at the place where one severs the horn and blood flows. There the horn is alive with the flesh — and it joins.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121a.14', refLabel: '121a:14' },
    ];

    const BIRD_ART = `
      <svg viewBox="0 0 400 180" class="h-full w-full" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#4a5170" stroke-width="2">
        <path d="M18 52 Q60 20 105 34 Q150 48 150 90 Q150 140 100 150 Q60 158 40 130" />
        <path d="M18 52 Q40 44 60 50" />
        <path d="M60 50 Q40 58 24 64 Q44 66 62 62" />
        <circle cx="88" cy="52" r="4" fill="#4a5170" />
        <path d="M150 90 Q220 70 285 92 Q330 108 330 130" />
        <path d="M330 130 Q310 150 285 156 M330 130 Q330 155 318 166 M330 130 Q348 150 342 164" stroke-width="2.5" />
        <path d="M285 92 Q300 70 336 66" stroke-dasharray="3 4" />
      </svg>`;
    const BEAST_ART = `
      <svg viewBox="0 0 400 180" class="h-full w-full" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#4a5170" stroke-width="2">
        <path d="M150 70 Q150 140 200 158 Q250 140 250 70 Q225 52 200 52 Q175 52 150 70 Z" />
        <path d="M150 70 Q110 60 78 26 Q104 44 148 52" />
        <path d="M250 70 Q290 60 322 26 Q296 44 252 52" />
        <circle cx="180" cy="88" r="4" fill="#4a5170" />
        <circle cx="220" cy="88" r="4" fill="#4a5170" />
        <path d="M186 132 Q200 140 214 132" />
        <path d="M296 52 Q304 58 300 66" stroke-dasharray="3 4" />
      </svg>`;

    const panelsEl = document.getElementById('probe-panels');
    const probeCardEl = document.getElementById('probe-card');
    const PANELS = [
      { key: 'bird', title: 'The bird — beak & talons', src: 'Teharot 1:2, read here', art: BIRD_ART },
      { key: 'beast', title: 'The beast — horns', src: 'our mishna', art: BEAST_ART },
    ];
    PANELS.forEach((p) => {
      const wrap = document.createElement('div');
      wrap.className = 'rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] p-3';
      wrap.innerHTML = `
        <p class="px-1 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">${p.title} <span class="normal-case tracking-normal">(${p.src})</span></p>
        <div class="art relative mt-2 h-44 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-[#0a0b14]">${p.art}</div>`;
      const art = wrap.querySelector('.art');
      PINS.filter((pin) => pin.panel === p.key).forEach((pin) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = 'pin';
        b.id = `pin-${pin.id}`;
        b.style.left = `${pin.x}%`;
        b.style.top = `${pin.y}%`;
        b.textContent = String(pin.n);
        b.setAttribute('aria-label', `Pin ${pin.n}: ${pin.label}`);
        b.addEventListener('click', () => openProbe(pin));
        art.appendChild(b);
      });
      panelsEl.appendChild(wrap);
    });

    const probeState = {}; // id -> 'done'
    let currentPin = null;
    function openProbe(pin) {
      if (probeState[pin.id] === 'done') return;
      if (currentPin && probeState[currentPin.id] !== 'done') {
        document.getElementById(`pin-${currentPin.id}`).dataset.state = '';
      }
      currentPin = pin;
      document.getElementById(`pin-${pin.id}`).dataset.state = 'open';
      probeCardEl.innerHTML = `
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#a78bfa]/40 bg-[#141830] p-4">
          <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.violet}">pin ${pin.n}</p>
          <h3 class="cormorant mt-0.5 text-lg font-bold ${C.text}">${pin.label}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm ${C.dim}">Does this part join with the flesh toward the egg-bulk of food impurity?</p>
          <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
            <button data-v="joins" class="gate-btn rounded-xl border border-[#f0954f]/50 bg-[#171a2b] px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold ${C.ember}">It joins</button>
            <button data-v="wood" class="gate-btn rounded-xl border border-[#9db1c7]/40 bg-[#171a2b] px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold ${C.bone}">Merely wood</button>
          </div>
          <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#0a0b14] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>`;
      const card = probeCardEl.firstElementChild;
      const reveal = card.querySelector('.reveal');
      let firstTry = true, settled = false;
      card.querySelectorAll('button[data-v]').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (settled) return;
          const right = (btn.dataset.v === 'joins') === pin.joins;
          reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
          if (right) {
            settled = true;
            probeState[pin.id] = 'done';
            const pinEl = document.getElementById(`pin-${pin.id}`);
            pinEl.dataset.state = pin.joins ? 'joins' : 'wood';
            pinEl.textContent = pin.joins ? '✚' : '✕';
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${pin.joins ? C.ember : C.bone}">${pin.joins ? '✚ It joins.' : '✕ Merely wood.'}</b>
              <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">${pin.he}</span> — ${pin.why}
              <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef(pin.ref, pin.refLabel)}</span>`;
            bump(firstTry);
          } else {
            firstTry = false;
            card.classList.remove('shake'); void card.offsetWidth; card.classList.add('shake');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.red}">The Gemara objects.</b> Try the other ruling.`;
          }
        });
      });
      const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      probeCardEl.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    }

    // =====================================================================
    // Act II — the threshold
    // =====================================================================
    const GATES = [
      { v: 'living', label: '🔥 The Living Gate', cls: `border-[#f0954f]/50 ${C.ember}` },
      { v: 'dead', label: '🌫️ The Dead Gate', cls: `border-[#9db1c7]/40 ${C.bone}` },
      { v: 'none', label: '🚫 No gate — the slaughter fails', cls: `border-[#565d78] ${C.mute}` },
    ];
    const THRESHOLD = [
      { q: 'While it twitches — can its flesh take on the impurity of food?',
        a: 'dead',
        why: `Yes: <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">מְטַמְּאָה טוּמְאַת אֳכָלִין</span> — the valid slaughter has already made it food, so for this law it has crossed to the dead side. (Per the Sages Rav Asi cites, it still needs intent that it be food and contact with liquid from elsewhere — its own slaughter-blood doesn't render it susceptible, since that blood flowed from a valid slaughter.)`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.7', refLabel: '121b:7' },
      { q: 'While it twitches — does it impart the impurity of an animal carcass?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `<span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">אֲבָל לֹא טוּמְאַת נְבֵלוֹת</span> — not while it twitches. A carcass must be dead, and this animal's soul has not yet departed.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.7', refLabel: '121b:7' },
      { q: 'A whole limb separates from it. How do we judge that limb?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `<span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">אֵבֶר הַפּוֹרֵשׁ מִמֶּנָּה כְּפוֹרֵשׁ מִן הַחַי</span> — like a limb parted from a living animal, and such a limb imparts carcass impurity. The doorway animal counts as alive for its parts.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.8', refLabel: '121b:8' },
      { q: 'Mere flesh — no bone — separates from it. Is that flesh impure?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `<span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">כְּבָשָׂר הַפּוֹרֵשׁ מִן הַחַי</span> — like flesh parted from the living, which imparts no impurity at all. Alive again.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.8', refLabel: '121b:8' },
      { q: 'That separated flesh — may a ben Noach eat it once the animal finally dies?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `<span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְאָסוּר לִבְנֵי נֹחַ, וַאֲפִילּוּ לְאַחַר שֶׁתֵּצֵא נַפְשָׁהּ</span> — forbidden, even after the soul departs. It parted from a living animal, and it remains "a limb from the living" forever.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.8', refLabel: '121b:8' },
      { q: 'May the gentile it was slaughtered for eat from it while it still twitches — according to Rabbi Yoḥanan?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `<span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">יֶשְׁנָהּ לְאֵבָרִים</span> — the prohibition of a limb from the living still applies; it is not yet dead. Ḥizkiyya disagreed (valid slaughter = dead), but Rabbi Elazar rules: take Rabbi Yoḥanan's opinion in your hand, for Rav Oshaya's baraita supports him. Rabbi Zeira saves Ḥizkiyya with this daf's motto: it left the category of the living — but never entered the category of the dead.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.6', refLabel: '121b:6' },
      { q: 'It lies twitching under one roof with a corpse, with swallowed items in its belly. Does it shield them from the corpse’s impurity, as a living animal would?',
        a: 'dead',
        why: `Abaye rules stringently: <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">אֵינָהּ מַצֶּלֶת עַל הַבְּלוּעִים שֶׁבְּתוֹכָהּ</span> — it does not save them, for it already takes the impurity of food. For this law, treat it as dead.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.21', refLabel: '121b:21' },
      { q: 'One who commits bestiality with it — liable, as with a living animal?',
        a: 'living',
        why: `Abaye's twin stringency: <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְהָרוֹבְעָהּ חַיָּיב</span> — liable, for it does not impart carcass impurity; for this law it is still alive. One animal, one moment — Abaye rules it dead for the swallowed items and alive for this, stringent in both directions.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.21', refLabel: '121b:21' },
      { q: 'Only one siman was cut — or a majority of one — and it twitches.',
        a: 'none',
        why: `The doorway collapses: the slaughter is invalid, so nothing has changed — it imparts no impurity whatsoever while it twitches. It is simply a living animal, dying.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.9', refLabel: '121b:9' },
      { q: 'He did not slaughter at all — he stabbed it (nechira), and it twitches.',
        a: 'none',
        why: `Stabbing is no slaughter. No gate opens: no food impurity, no carcass impurity — no impurity at all, until it actually dies and becomes a carcass like any other.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.121b.9', refLabel: '121b:9' },
    ];

    const orb = document.getElementById('orb');
    const orbCaption = document.getElementById('orb-caption');
    const tallies = { living: 0, dead: 0 };
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    function tug(dir) {
      if (dir === 'none') {
        orb.classList.add('dimmed');
        orbCaption.textContent = 'The doorway collapses — with no valid slaughter there is nothing between the gates.';
        setTimeout(() => { orb.classList.remove('dimmed'); }, reduceMotion ? 0 : 1200);
        return;
      }
      tallies[dir]++;
      document.getElementById(`tally-${dir}`).textContent = String(tallies[dir]);
      orbCaption.textContent = dir === 'living'
        ? 'It leans toward the Living Gate… and drifts back to the threshold.'
        : 'It leans toward the Dead Gate… and drifts back to the threshold.';
      if (reduceMotion) return;
      const dx = dir === 'living' ? '-80px' : '80px';
      orb.style.transform = `translate(calc(-50% + ${dx}), -50%)`;
      setTimeout(() => { orb.style.transform = 'translate(-50%, -50%)'; }, 900);
    }

    const thresholdEl = document.getElementById('threshold-cards');
    THRESHOLD.forEach((t, i) => {
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] p-4';
      card.innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">ruling ${i + 1} of ${THRESHOLD.length}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold leading-snug ${C.text}">${t.q}</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3"></div>
        <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#0a0b14] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      const btnWrap = card.querySelector('.grid');
      const reveal = card.querySelector('.reveal');
      let firstTry = true, settled = false;
      GATES.forEach((g) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = `gate-btn rounded-xl border bg-[#171a2b] px-3 py-2.5 text-left text-sm font-bold ${g.cls}`;
        b.textContent = g.label;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (settled) return;
          if (g.v === t.a) {
            settled = true;
            tug(t.a);
            const tone = t.a === 'living' ? C.ember : t.a === 'dead' ? C.bone : C.mute;
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${tone}">${t.a === 'living' ? '🔥 The Living Gate.' : t.a === 'dead' ? '🌫️ The Dead Gate.' : '🚫 No gate.'}</b>
              ${t.why} <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef(t.ref, t.refLabel)}</span>`;
            btnWrap.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => { if (x !== b) x.style.opacity = '0.35'; });
            bump(firstTry);
          } else {
            firstTry = false;
            card.classList.remove('shake'); void card.offsetWidth; card.classList.add('shake');
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.red}">The daf rules otherwise.</b> Choose again.`;
          }
        });
        btnWrap.appendChild(b);
      });
      thresholdEl.appendChild(card);
    });

    // epilogue card (not scored)
    const epi = document.createElement('div');
    epi.className = 'rounded-2xl border border-[#a78bfa]/30 bg-[#141830] p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed';
    epi.innerHTML = `
      <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.violet}">the elder at the door</p>
      <p class="mt-1.5 ${C.dim}">Rabbi Elazar asked: this shadow-slaughter — must it be flawless? If the slaughterer paused
      (<i>shehiyya</i>) or pressed the knife (<i>derasa</i>), does the animal still enter the doorway? A certain elder
      answered in Rabbi Yoḥanan's name: it must be <b class="${C.text}">a valid slaughter in every detail, like a Jew
      slaughtering a kosher animal</b> — down to inspecting the knife first (Rav Shmuel bar Yitzḥak).
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef('Chullin.121b.17', '121b:17–18')}</span></p>`;
    thresholdEl.appendChild(epi);

    // =====================================================================
    // Act III — the collectors
    // =====================================================================
    const collectorsEl = document.getElementById('collectors');

    const cCard = document.createElement('div');
    cCard.className = 'rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] p-4';
    cCard.innerHTML = `
      <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">rabbi yehuda's rule</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold leading-snug ${C.text}">An olive-bulk of alal lies heaped in one place —
        <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">הָאָלָל הַמְכוּנָּס</span>. Which gathering makes it impart carcass impurity?</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs ${C.mute}">Rabbi Yehuda: one who touches it and then eats consecrated food or enters the Temple is liable to karet. But Rav Huna adds a condition…</p>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3"></div>
      <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#0a0b14] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
    const COLLECTORS = [
      { id: 'adult', label: '🧍 A grown person gathered it', ok: true },
      { id: 'child', label: '🧒 A child gathered it', ok: false },
      { id: 'wind', label: '💨 The wind heaped it up', ok: false },
    ];
    {
      const wrap = cCard.querySelector('.grid');
      const reveal = cCard.querySelector('.reveal');
      let firstTry = true, settled = false;
      COLLECTORS.forEach((c) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = `gate-btn rounded-xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#171a2b] px-3 py-2.5 text-left text-sm font-bold ${C.text}`;
        b.textContent = c.label;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (settled) return;
          if (c.ok) {
            settled = true;
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.ember}">Only the person of da'at.</b>
              <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְהוּא שֶׁכִּנְּסוֹ</span> — Rav Huna: the rule holds only when a
              halakhically competent person collected it. The gathering itself is the statement "this is food to me."
              A child's heap or the wind's heap declares nothing, and the alal stays nullified.
              <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef('Chullin.121a.5', '121a:5')}, ${sef('Chullin.121b.22', '121b:22')}</span>`;
            wrap.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => { if (x !== b) x.style.opacity = '0.35'; });
            bump(firstTry);
          } else {
            firstTry = false;
            cCard.classList.remove('shake'); void cCard.offsetWidth; cCard.classList.add('shake');
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.red}">No da'at, no verdict.</b> That heap declares nothing. Choose again.`;
          }
        });
        wrap.appendChild(b);
      });
    }
    collectorsEl.appendChild(cCard);

    const hCard = document.createElement('div');
    hCard.className = 'rounded-2xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#11131f] p-4';
    hCard.innerHTML = `
      <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">rav huna's last word</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold leading-snug ${C.text}">Two pieces of carcass flesh, each half an olive-bulk, cling to the hide. Together they make the full measure. Impure?</p>
      <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2"></div>
      <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#252a42] bg-[#0a0b14] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
    {
      const wrap = hCard.querySelector('.grid');
      const reveal = hCard.querySelector('.reveal');
      let firstTry = true, settled = false;
      [
        { label: 'They join — carcass impurity', ok: false, cls: `border-[#e05e63]/50 ${C.red}` },
        { label: 'The hide swallows them', ok: true, cls: `border-[#9db1c7]/40 ${C.bone}` },
      ].forEach((o) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = `gate-btn rounded-xl border bg-[#171a2b] px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold ${o.cls}`;
        b.textContent = o.label;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (settled) return;
          if (o.ok) {
            settled = true;
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.bone}">The hide nullifies them.</b>
              <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">הָעוֹר מְבַטְּלָן</span> — Rav Huna: the hide, which imparts no
              carcass impurity, cancels the half-measures riding on it. The daf ends where it began: what clings to the
              hide follows the hide.
              <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef('Chullin.121b.23', '121b:23')}</span>`;
            wrap.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => { if (x !== b) x.style.opacity = '0.35'; });
            bump(firstTry);
          } else {
            firstTry = false;
            hCard.classList.remove('shake'); void hCard.offsetWidth; hCard.classList.add('shake');
            reveal.classList.remove('hidden');
            reveal.innerHTML = `<b class="${C.red}">Not so.</b> Remember whose back they ride on.`;
          }
        });
        wrap.appendChild(b);
      });
    }
    collectorsEl.appendChild(hCard);

    // =====================================================================
    // Finale
    // =====================================================================
    function maybeFinale() {
      if (answered < TOTAL) return;
      const f = document.getElementById('finale');
      let grade, note;
      if (score >= 17) { grade = '🕯️ Keeper of the Threshold'; note = 'You ruled the doorway like Abaye — stringent toward both gates at once, and never once pretending the animal had picked a side.'; }
      else if (score >= 12) { grade = '🚪 One foot on the sill'; note = 'Take Rabbi Yoḥanan\'s opinion in your hand — Rav Oshaya taught in accordance with you, mostly.'; }
      else if (score >= 6) { grade = '🌫️ Lost in the doorway'; note = 'Like Ḥizkiyya before Rabbi Zeira rescued him: a defensible position, but the baraita ran the other way. Walk the threshold again.'; }
      else { grade = '💨 Gathered by the wind'; note = 'A heap without da\'at declares nothing — Rav Huna would say your verdicts don\'t yet count as gathered. Learn the daf and return.'; }
      f.classList.remove('hidden');
      f.innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] ${C.mute}">where you stand</p>
        <p class="cormorant mt-2 text-2xl font-bold ${C.ember}">${grade}</p>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">${note}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm ${C.text}">${score} of ${TOTAL} verdicts on the first try. The gates tallied
          <b class="${C.ember}">${tallies.living} living</b> and <b class="${C.bone}">${tallies.dead} dead</b> —
          and still the animal stands between them.</p>
        <p class="frank mt-3 text-lg font-bold ${C.violet}" dir="rtl" lang="he">יָצְתָה מִכְּלַל חַיָּה, וְלִכְלַל מֵתָה לֹא בָּאת</p>`;
      const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      f.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
